# uv
.python-version-local

# ML artifacts and datasets.
# Model bundles are pickle-based and environment-specific, and the registry index
# records absolute paths; both are reproduced by `aeropulse-ml train`. Committing
# them would also put executable pickles in version control.
models/
data/

# Exception: the population reference layer is source, not a generated dataset.
# It is small (28 district points), it is an input to every exposure number, and
# `data/` above would otherwise exclude it silently — which would leave a fresh
# clone falling back to a constant density for every cell while still reporting
# `population_measured: false` only in places nobody reads.
!libs/geospatial/aeropulse_geospatial/data/
!libs/geospatial/aeropulse_geospatial/data/*.json

# Notebook research artifacts. `data/` above already covers the datasets, but it
# did NOT cover artifacts/, which is how a 1.5 GB pm25_regime_aware_bundle.joblib
# reached git history in 8b71dce. Every file under these paths is regenerated by
# re-running the notebook that wrote it.
AeroPulse_ML_Notebooks/**/artifacts/
artifacts/
catboost_info/

# Notebook checkpoints
.ipynb_checkpoints/
.ipython/

# Knowledge-graph build output (regenerable)
graphify-out/

# ---------------------------------------------------------------------------
# Belt and braces: ban the FILE TYPES, not just the directories.
# ---------------------------------------------------------------------------
# The directory rules above are the primary defence, but they only work when an
# artifact lands where it was expected to. The 1.5 GB bundle in 8b71dce was
# written to a path nobody had listed yet. GitHub hard-rejects any single file
# over 100 MB, and that rejection blocks the whole push, so the cost of one
# escape is the entire branch. No tracked file in this repo uses any extension
# below (verified: `git ls-files` matches zero), so these cost nothing today and
# catch the next unplanned output path.
*.joblib
*.pkl
*.pickle
*.parquet
**/*.parquet
*.feather
*.npy
*.npz
*.h5
*.hdf5
*.onnx
*.pt
*.pth
*.ckpt
*.safetensors
*.tflite
*.model
*.bin

# Bulk data interchange. Fixtures are JSON and stay tracked; these are the
# formats research output actually arrives in.
*.csv
*.tsv
*.csv.gz
*.jsonl
*.arrow

# Archives
*.zip
*.tar
*.tar.gz
*.tgz
*.7z

# Experiment trackers and local caches
mlruns/
.mlflow/
lightning_logs/
wandb/
optuna.db
*.sqlite
*.sqlite3
*.db-journal

# Raw provider caches written by the acquisition notebooks
**/data/pm25/raw/
**/raw/stations/
